{#- Nowcasting note — English template.

Context variables:
    run_date         str   "2026-10-01"
    target_quarter   str   "2026Q3"
    horizon          str   "nowcast_m3"
    new_nowcast      float  GDP y/y estimate
    old_nowcast      float  previous estimate (or None)
    total_change     float  change in pp (or None)
    revision_effect  float  pp
    news_effect      float  pp
    reest_effect     float  pp
    top_news         list[NewsItem]  up to 5 top drivers
    grouped_impacts  dict[str, float]  group -> pp
    sectors          list[SectorContribution]
    bridge_gdp       float  bridge-equation GDP (for comparison)
    has_decomposition bool
    ytd              dict  year-to-date context (None in old callers): with it new_nowcast,
                           old_nowcast and the effects are year to date, as Uzstat publishes
-#}
{%- set horizon_label = {
    "forecast": "forecast",
    "nowcast_m1": "early estimate (month 1)",
    "nowcast_m2": "estimate (month 2)",
    "nowcast_m3": "estimate (month 3)",
    "backcast": "backcast",
}.get(horizon, horizon) -%}

{%- if ytd %}
{%- set ordinal = {1: "first", 2: "second", 3: "third", 4: "fourth"}[ytd.quarter] -%}
As of {{ run_date }}, the {{ horizon_label }} of GDP growth for {{ ytd.span_en }} {{ ytd.year }} is {{ "%.1f"|format(new_nowcast) }}% y/y, on the cumulative basis Uzstat publishes.
{%- if ytd.quarter > 1 %} The {{ ordinal }} quarter alone is estimated at {{ "%.1f"|format(ytd.quarter_value) }}%{% if ytd.known_through %}; Uzstat's figure for {{ ytd.known_span_en }} is {{ "%.1f"|format(ytd.known_value) }}%{% endif %}.{% endif %}
{%- else %}
As of {{ run_date }}, the {{ horizon_label }} for {{ target_quarter }} GDP growth is {{ "%.1f"|format(new_nowcast) }}% y/y.
{%- endif %}
{%- if has_decomposition and old_nowcast is not none %} {% if total_change|round(1) == 0 %}This is unchanged from the previous estimate of {{ "%.1f"|format(old_nowcast) }}%.{% else %}This is {{ "%.1f"|format(total_change|abs) }} pp {{ "higher" if total_change > 0 else "lower" }} than the previous estimate of {{ "%.1f"|format(old_nowcast) }}%.{% endif %}
{%- if ytd and ytd.earlier_effect|abs >= 0.05 %} Of the change, {{ "%+.1f"|format(ytd.earlier_effect) }} pp comes from Uzstat's figures for the earlier quarters of the year (or the model's estimate of them).{% endif %}
{%- endif %}

{%- if has_decomposition and top_news %}

The change reflects
{%- set pos_groups = grouped_impacts|dictsort|selectattr("1", "gt", 0.05)|list -%}
{%- set neg_groups = grouped_impacts|dictsort|selectattr("1", "lt", -0.05)|list -%}
{%- if pos_groups %} upward pressure from {{ pos_groups|map(attribute="0")|join(", ") }}{% endif -%}
{%- if pos_groups and neg_groups %}, partly offset by{% elif neg_groups %} downward pressure from{% endif -%}
{%- if neg_groups %} {{ neg_groups|map(attribute="0")|join(", ") }}{% endif -%}
. The largest single drivers are {{ top_news[:3]|map(attribute="label")|join(", ") }}.
{%- endif %}

{%- if sectors %}

By sector, the main contributors are
{%- for s in sectors[:4] %} {{ s.label }} ({{ "%.1f"|format(s.growth_yoy) }}% y/y, {{ "%+.1f"|format(s.contribution_pp) }} pp){{ "," if not loop.last else "." }}{% endfor %}
{%- endif %}
